> _note: this might be optimizing for a rare case, since Next already aggressively preloads linked pages._

From side discussion with @spanicker - maybe consider using preload to start fetching the route chunk in parallel with its dependencies here?

```js
let dependenciesReady = Promise.resolve();
if (urlsToLoad.length > 0) {
  // get the route chunk loading in parallel with its dependencies:
  // (but don't wait for the preload to finish, since that would be unnecessarily serial)
  this.preload(route);
  dependenciesReady = Promise.all(urlsToLoad.map(this.loadDependency))
}
this.loadingRoutes[route] = true
dependenciesReady.then(() => {
  this.loadScript(route)
})
```

